    transport failure or [38;5;153m5xx[39m. Keeping the [38;5;153m{success}[39m shape means the existing handler at [38;5;153mapp.js:23[39m barely changes.
  - A failed login [1mnever clobbers an existing valid memo[0m — a bad re-auth attempt shouldn't log you out of the session
    you already have.
  - [1m[38;5;153mAuth.getUser[0m resolves [38;5;153mnull[39m on [38;5;153m401[39m. That's an answer, not an error.
  - [1m[38;5;153mAuth.getUser[39m on network failure rejects and clears the in-flight memo without caching.[0m This is the subtle one and
    worth its own line in the spec: if a transient blip were cached as [38;5;153mnull[39m, every consumer on the page would render
    logged-out until reload, and the UI would be lying about a session that's perfectly alive. Failure must stay
    retryable.

  [1mSection 5 — Testing and tooling[0m

  The [1mtest fake[0m is a [38;5;153mfetch[39m stub holding a fake session store, honoring [38;5;153mcredentials: "include"[39m the way a browser would.
  It covers: login success and credential rejection; [38;5;153m/me[39m rehydration after a simulated reload; N concurrent [38;5;153mgetUser()[39m
  callers producing exactly one request; the memo-overwrite ordering from section 1; network failure staying uncached;
  logout clearing state.

  The repo has no test runner, no linter, no formatter, and no [38;5;153mscripts[39m in [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m. Setting these up is cheapest
  now, before any of this code exists, so one question on that:
